<article class="env-lemma" id="01SO">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01SO">Lemma <span data-tag="01SO">29.13.5</span>.</a> The base change of a quasi-affine morphism is quasi-affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to S$ be a quasi-affine morphism. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01SM" data-tag="01SM">29.13.3</a> above we can find a quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebras $\mathcal{A}$ and a quasi-compact open immersion $X \to \underline{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}}_ S(\mathcal{A})$ over $S$. Let $g : S' \to S$ be any morphism. Denote $f' : X_{S'} = S' \times _ S X \to S'$ the base change of $f$. Since the base change of a quasi-compact open immersion is a quasi-compact open immersion we see that $X_{S'} \to \underline{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}}_{S'}(g^*\mathcal{A})$ is a quasi-compact open immersion (we have used Schemes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/01K5" data-tag="01K5">26.19.3</a> and <a href="/tag/01JY" data-tag="01JY">26.18.2</a> and Constructions, Lemma <a href="/tag/01LX" data-tag="01LX">27.4.6</a>). By Lemma <a href="/tag/01SM" data-tag="01SM">29.13.3</a> again we conclude that $X_{S'} \to S'$ is quasi-affine. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>